\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Christ Jesus lay in death's strong bands
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj For our offences given;
\par But now at God's right hand He stands,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj And brings us life from heaven:
\par Wherefore, let us Joyfully be,
\par And sing to God right thankfully,
\par Loud songs of Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  It was a strange and dreadful strife,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 When Life and Death contended;
\par The victory remained with life,
\par The reign of Death was ended:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Stript of power, no more he reigns;
\par An empty form alone remains:
\par His sting is lost forever,
\par 
\par \pard\fi-360\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par     3.  So let us keep the festival,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0      Whereto the lord invites us:
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Christ is Himself the joy of us,
\par The Sun that warms and lights us:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par By His grace He doth impart
\par Eternal sunshine to the heart;
\par The night of sin is ended,
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then let us feast this Easter day,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 On the true Bread of Heaven.
\par The word of grace hath purged away;
\par The old and wicked heaven;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Christ alone our souls He will feed,
\par He is our lamb and drink indeed,
\par \pard         Faith lives upon no other, \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

